
---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f4efe6" />
    <title>About — The Listening Room</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="The thinking behind The Listening Room, an independent personal music journal by Isaiah Wilkins."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="The Listening Room home">
        The Listening Room<span class="period">.</span>
      </a>
      <p class="masthead-note">AN INDEPENDENT MUSIC JOURNAL</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="/">LATEST ISSUE</a>
      <a href="/archive/">THE ARCHIVE</a>
      <a href="/playlists/">PLAYLISTS</a>
      <a href="/album-reviews/">ALBUM REVIEWS</a>
      <a href="/listener-requests/">LISTENER REQUESTS</a>
      <a href="/about/" aria-current="page">ABOUT</a>
    </nav>

    <main class="category-page about-page">
      <header class="category-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">A NOTE FROM THE EDITOR</p>
        <h1>Music is a way of <em>seeing.</em></h1>
        <p>
          The Listening Room is an independent music journal by Isaiah
          Wilkins, built around a simple idea: sometimes you hear something
          in a song that makes perfect sense to you, even when someone else
          hears it differently.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="playlist-list">
        <article class="playlist-entry">
          <p class="playlist-number">01</p>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">THE PERSPECTIVE</p>
            <h2>It's about the feeling behind it all.</h2>
            <p>
              I'm interested in finding the reasons a song works for me:
              the details, choices, and unexpected connections that draw me
              back. Music doesn't need to fit a particular genre or mood to
              belong here. What matters is the experience of listening and
              discovering why it resonates.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="playlist-entry">
          <p class="playlist-number">02</p>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">THE PUBLICATION</p>
            <h2>A record of what stayed with me.</h2>
            <p>
              Each monthly issue captures a period of listening through
              playlists, album reviews, writing, and photography. The
              selections don't have to sound alike. Each one earns its place
              for its own reasons, and every issue becomes a time capsule of
              that moment.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="playlist-entry">
          <p class="playlist-number">03</p>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">LISTEN ALONG</p>
            <h2>Come in with your own ears.</h2>
            <p>
              This is a personal perspective, not the final word on music.
              Take what resonates, disagree where you like, and listen for
              the things you might have missed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">The Listening Room<span class="period">.</span></a>
      <p>MADE TO BE LISTENED TO.</p>
      <p>© 2026 THE LISTENING ROOM</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
